==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|snīdan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*snīþaną||to cut}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*sneyt-||to cut}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|snijden||to cut, carve, intersect}}, {{etyl|nds|-}} {{m|nds|snieden||to cut}}, dialectal {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|snithe||to cut}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|snida||to carve, engrave}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{m|is|sníða||to trim, tailor}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃnaɪ̯dn̩/|/ˈʃnaɪ̯dən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-schneiden.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=1|schneidet|schnitt|geschnitten|past subjunctive=schnitte}}

# {{label|de|transitive}} to [[cut]]; to [[carve]]; to [[slice]]
# {{label|de|transitive}} to [[pare]]; to [[clip]]; to [[mow]]; to [[prune]]; to [[trim]]
# {{label|de|transitive|driving|figuratively}} to cut (someone) off; to cut in on (someone)
# {{label|de|transitive|film}} to [[edit]]
# {{label|de|transitive|or|reflexive}} to [[intersect]]
#: ''Die beiden Geraden '''schneiden''' sich.'' — “Both streets intersect.”
# {{label|de|reflexive}} to [[cut]] (oneself)
# {{label|de|reflexive|colloquial}} to [[delude]] (oneself); to become mistaken
# to [[avoid]] somebody (to cut someone)
<!-- Are there any intransitive senses? -->

